Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] overlay restore: loud failure, failed id not recorded

Follow-up to 0008. The host loaders called dw3_overlay_restore and ignored
its result, then stored the id in OVERLAY_LOADER.mode / .subOverlay anyway.
A file id that is not in the host overlay table therefore only printed the
`kind=unknown UNKNOWN` marker, and the latch claimed it was loaded.

Both loaders now go through dw3_overlay_load_mode / dw3_overlay_load_sub
(port/overlays/overlay_host.c), which keep the PS1 rule (same id: no-op,
globals preserved; new mode: sub latch reset to -1) and, on a failed
restore, log a `dw3: ERROR overlay restore failed` line, abort in strict
mode (DW3_OVERLAY_STRICT=1, any DW3_REPLAY run, the Switch replay build),
and set the latch to -1 so the id is not recorded as loaded.

Non-PORT_HOST code is unchanged.

--- a/src/engine/system/overlay.c
+++ b/src/engine/system/overlay.c
@@ -246,14 +246,12 @@
      * Static overlay model (P2.6): restore initial .data and zero .bss for
      * MODE_OVERLAY_FILES[id] only when the mode index changes. Same mode
      * re-entry preserves overlay globals (PS1 memcpy-skip semantics).
+     * A failed restore (file id not in the host table) is logged as an
+     * error, aborts in strict/replay runs, and leaves the latch at -1
+     * instead of recording the id as loaded (port/overlays, patch 0060).
      */
-    if (OVERLAY_LOADER.mode != id) {
-        OVERLAY_LOADER.mode = id;
-        OVERLAY_LOADER.subOverlay = -1;
-        if (MODE_OVERLAY_FILES[id] != 0) {
-            (void)dw3_overlay_restore(MODE_OVERLAY_FILES[id]);
-        }
-    }
+    (void)dw3_overlay_load_mode(&OVERLAY_LOADER.mode, &OVERLAY_LOADER.subOverlay, id,
+                                MODE_OVERLAY_FILES[id]);
 #else
     u8 *src;
     void *dst;
@@ -271,10 +269,8 @@
 /* Copies a file to the second overlay area (SUB_OVERLAY_ADDRESS) */
 void loadSubOverlay(s32 id) {
 #if PORT_HOST
-    if (OVERLAY_LOADER.subOverlay != id) {
-        OVERLAY_LOADER.subOverlay = id;
-        (void)dw3_overlay_restore(id);
-    }
+    /* Same id: no-op. Failed restore: not recorded (see loadModeOverlay). */
+    (void)dw3_overlay_load_sub(&OVERLAY_LOADER.subOverlay, id);
 #else
     u8 *src;
     void *dst;
